PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains an unbroken, unanimous 8–0 consensus supporting Choice C (None of the choices). Metastatic Stage IV melanoma with cardiac tamponade requires guideline-directed immune checkpoint inhibition or targeted therapy, alongside definitive pericardial drainage, none of which are listed. Cytotoxic chemotherapy is obsolete, immunosuppression is harmful, and diuretics are contraindicated due to preload dependence. The strategy remains unchanged to uphold Choice C in the subsequent rounds.
}

